Z||000000||Jefrysuko||12-18-2001||03:11 AM||||Ok here's the deal guy's.  I am involved in a design competition here at my school and we build and race what is called a Mini Baja car.  Like this....<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://eng-council.cen.uiuc.edu/soc/sae/baja/photos/2000/baja%20sponsorshot.jpg">  <P>So what I need to know is about rear axles.  We found that we can get a 2" cut spline (sp?) aluminum axle to work easily with our setup.  I don't know if this is from a mini sprint car or a midget (not sure yet).  The questions we have are about reliability.  Some members of the team are concerned that the cut splines are going to fatigue easier than rolled splines or that the aluminum is going to not be strong enough.<P>So if anyone has some experience with a similar type of axle please bring on the stories.  I will try to provide more information as I get it.<p>[This message has been edited by Jefrysuko (edited 12-18-2001).]||||reg||1
